cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use play-along in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "play-along: turn any song into a falling-notes play-along video and practice player"
authors:
  - given-names: "Yogesh"
    family-names: "Kumar"
    alias: "yogesh-iitj"
    website: "https://github.com/yogesh-iitj"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/working-codes-demo/play-along"
url: "https://working-codes-demo.github.io/play-along/"
abstract: >-
  Turns any recording or YouTube link into per-instrument notes, a falling-notes
  play-along video with every instrument in its own colour, a multi-track MIDI file
  and a browser practice player with solo, mute, synth playback, slow-down and A-B loops.
  Runs on a laptop CPU or Apple Silicon.
keywords:
  - music transcription
  - audio to MIDI
  - music education
  - piano
  - visualization
